|HTTP Status Codes|

200 — OK --Request successful.
Request successful.

201 — Created

Resource successfully created.
Usually after POST.

204 — No Content
Operation succeeded but response has no body.
Often used with DELETE or certain updates.

400 — Bad Request
Client sent invalid data.
Example:

{
    "age": "hello"
}
when age should be a number.

401 — Unauthorized
Authentication is missing/invalid.

Think:
"I don't know who you are."

403 — Forbidden
User is authenticated but doesn't have permission.

Think:
"I know who you are, but you're not allowed."

404 — Not Found
Resource doesn't exist.
GET /customers/99999  

409 — Conflict
Request conflicts with current resource state.

Example:
Creating a customer with an email that must be unique.

500 — Internal Server Error
Something went wrong on the server.

502 — Bad Gateway
A server acting as a gateway/proxy received an invalid response from an upstream server.

503 — Service Unavailable
Server/service is temporarily unavailable.
