|Retry Logic|

Imagine:

API request
   ↓
Temporary failure
   ↓
Retry

A production system may use exponential backoff:

1 second
   ↓
2 seconds
   ↓
4 seconds
   ↓
8 seconds

Don't retry everything blindly.

For example:

401 → authentication problem

Repeated retries won't fix it.

But:

503 → temporary service unavailable

may be retryable.
